<h1>Shift-Or</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="stringMatching.html"><em>string matching</em></a> algorithm which keeps an <a href="array.html"><em>array</em></a> of bits, R, showing if <a href="prefix.html"><em>prefixes</em></a> of the <a href="pattern.html"><em>pattern</em></a> don't match at the current place.  Before searching, mismatch arrays are computed for each character in the <a href="alphabet.html"><em>alphabet</em></a> and saved in an array, S.  For the next position, with the character c, R = shift(R) <a href="or.html"><em>or</em></a> S[c].  If the last bit of R is 0, the pattern matches.
</p>


<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="http://www-igm.univ-mlv.fr/~lecroq/string/node6.html" target="_blank">explanation and code (C)</a>

